            <ArticleTitle>[Laparoscopic treatment of postoperative peritoneal adhesions].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49-51; discussion 51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>75 patients with postoperative peritoneal adhesions, complicated by a severe pain syndrome, were operated on during 2003-2006 yy. The preoperative use of the enzyme medication &lt;Collagenase KK&gt; in 28 patients allowed therefore the conduction of adequate laparoscopic adhesiolysis. There were no complications and recurrences registered at follow-up. The postoperative hospital stay averaged 3.7 days.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
